mapping "V4673.1" source="V4673" target="36198007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V4673 is a Swedish national 6-character extension of base ICD-10 code V467 = Car occupant
        injured in collision with other nonmotor vehicle, person on outside of vehicle injured in
        traffic accident (V46.7); the 6th character encodes the activity at time of accident (annan
        sysselsättning (other activity)). Source definition: same motor-vehicle accident event as the
        base code, with additional activity-context granularity that has no SNOMED CT representation.
        Target(s): SNOMED CT 444074 (36198007); SNOMED CT 4152175 (271579008). Why this target: the SNOMED CT
        concept(s) are the standard crosswalk targets for the base ICD-10 code (Athena SNOMED 271579008
        36198007); they fully subsume the accident event; the activity-context dimension is lost but the
        injury event semantics are fully covered, so the relationship is broader. Confidence (moderate):
        best available standard concept, defensible subsumption, but the source is a Swedish extension
        with an unspecified-activity axis that the standard vocabulary cannot represent.
        """
}
mapping "V4673.2" source="V4673" target="271579008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
}
